{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455271-converting-your-1e-game-to-2e","id":455271,"title":"Converting your 1E game to 2E.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-23T19:55:32-07:00","id":455271,"title":"Converting your 1E game to 2E.","content":"Any tips? We had been hesitant to convert to The God Machine/2nd Edition system initially. We took the Social Doors system and wanted to do beats but couldn't strike a balance between trait conversion.<br /> <br /> We're really far in the game so we can't just switch over everyone's gifts without major weirdness happening. What we've done is basically hybridized. We're using beats and doors. We've made it so that the tiered gifts in 1st Ed now cost 1 experience per dot level of the gift with no penalty for skipping, and unlocking the Technology gift in 1E counts as having it unlocked re:facets and so on. This was the biggest change we had to make. We haven't yet gone over to the defense and weapon system, because it seems weird and counter intuitive, though I'm starting to warm up to it.<br /> <br /> Anyone run into any other problems or made any houserules to aid in their conversions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T01:00:37-07:00","id":455532,"title":"","content":"I run a 1ed game with GMC rules and 2ed setting patches, no mechanics changes for werewolves. I see mostly the Gifts will be a big thing to rearrange, but to this date we only had handful of those.<br /> <br /> And perspective in rules shift is limited only to pause in the game - we did not played in few weeks and I do not see as players having major problems in character shift, if they have hazy memory of previous session.<br /> <br /> Changes in 2ed are mostly in detail, overall of game has left mostly the same. You still hunt things, you still can be 2,5 meters giant monster, you still are connected to Spirits World.<br /> <br /> As I see, changes are more like &quot;evolution&quot; not &quot;revolution&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T08:18:14-07:00","id":455838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455271-converting-your-1e-game-to-2e#post455271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any tips? We had been hesitant to convert to The God Machine/2nd Edition system initially. We took the Social Doors system and wanted to do beats but couldn't strike a balance between trait conversion.<br /> <br /> We're really far in the game so we can't just switch over everyone's gifts without major weirdness happening. What we've done is basically hybridized. We're using beats and doors. We've made it so that the tiered gifts in 1st Ed now cost 1 experience per dot level of the gift with no penalty for skipping, and unlocking the Technology gift in 1E counts as having it unlocked re:facets and so on. This was the biggest change we had to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting approach, makes sense. Personally, I would just allow everyone to reset their Gifts. Let them pick one Facet per dot of Renown (-1 of their primary if they're an Auspice + Tribe combination with the same favored Renown) chosen from any Gift List they previously had Gifts from, plus Pack Gifts since that doesn't have an obvious 1e analogue. If they still have fewer Facets than they previously had Gifts, let them chose additional Facets from their available Gifts until the total is equal. Your way is probably cleaner though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455271-converting-your-1e-game-to-2e#post455271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We haven't yet gone over to the defense and weapon system, because it seems weird and counter intuitive, though I'm starting to warm up to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counter-intuitive in what way? To me the 2e combat system is more intuitive. Weapons add actual damage instead of adding more dice and armor adds actual damage resistance instead of reducing your attacker's dice. The higher defense values due to adding Athletics to Defense I know bothered a lot of people, but I wouldn't exactly call it unintuitive, and it's easy to leave out if you don't like it. Just trying to get a feel for what you dislike about the changes to the combat system so I can give you better advice for your group's needs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455271-converting-your-1e-game-to-2e#post455271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone run into any other problems or made any houserules to aid in their conversions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been having some trouble converting Harmony. My guideline so far is to treat old Harmony 10 as new Harmony 5, then every 2 points below old 10 is one point away from 5, and I just eyeball which direction based on if the character seems more physical or spiritual overall. It kind of works, but it's very polarizing, and I wonder if anyone has a better system (besides &quot;just pick a number that seems about right&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-24-2015, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T08:53:35-07:00","id":455877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455271-converting-your-1e-game-to-2e?p=455838#post455838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Counter-intuitive in what way? To me the 2e combat system is more intuitive. Weapons add actual damage instead of adding more dice and armor adds actual damage resistance instead of reducing your attacker's dice. The higher defense values due to adding Athletics to Defense I know bothered a lot of people, but I wouldn't exactly call it unintuitive, and it's easy to leave out if you don't like it. Just trying to get a feel for what you dislike about the changes to the combat system so I can give you better advice for your group's needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see it as counter-intuitive as well... you can NEVER have a grazing shot in Second Edition. Ever. You either hit for full weapon damage (+ hits) or you don't. To me that is exceedingly counter-intuitive. Grazes are a thing, and they should be in the game (I know that some say to use Tilts and such for this). I also did not like the resulting reduction in DP's due to that particular change. Combat becomes way to static for my tastes (yeah, I know, I am weird), because the reduced DP's result in far fewer (but far more deadly) hits. I am one of those who did not see any issues with the combat system previously, where I feel it is FAR more dynamic (even without the Tilts and Conditions) than what we get in Second Edition. I am on an island on this, I know, but that is okay. You can only comment on what you know, and I find combat in 2nd Edition to be pretty boring, overall, in comparison to the previous edition (and no, I am not one of those who heavily supports the multiple attacks in 1st Edition, probably because we never really had much in the way of characters who practiced such things).<br /> <br /> I also don't particularly care for the Athletics additions to defense either. Yeah, I am one of those who are bothered by it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:45:58-07:00","id":455954,"title":"","content":"Sure, those are all reasons one might not like the combat changes, but I wouldn't describr them as counter-intuitive, except maybe the grazing blow thing. And wouldn't a grazing hit by definition not do damage? Just describe a near miss as a graze, easy peasy.<br /> <br /> Forgive me if I don't give advice for addressing your concerns about the system, Tymaeus, since I know you're perfectly happy using the 1e combat rules, it wouldn't benefit either of us. If Ameavanti posts their issues with the system, I will attempt to address them then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T11:05:30-07:00","id":456007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455271-converting-your-1e-game-to-2e?p=455954#post455954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, those are all reasons one might not like the combat changes, but I wouldn't describr them as counter-intuitive, except maybe the grazing blow thing. And wouldn't a grazing hit by definition not do damage? Just describe a near miss as a graze, easy peasy.<br /> <br /> Forgive me if I don't give advice for addressing your concerns about the system, Tymaeus, since I know you're perfectly happy using the 1e combat rules, it wouldn't benefit either of us. If Ameavanti posts their issues with the system, I will attempt to address them then.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, <i><b>Charlaquin</b></i>. It was just something that caused cognitive dissonance for me when GMC came out, and I thought it meshed well with what was said earlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T11:20:41-07:00","id":456023,"title":"","content":"For sure. It was a fair point, I just didn't want you to feel snubbed since I offered advice on transitioning to 2e combat and then didn't give any to you when you mentioned your grievances with it. I figured you probably weren't interested in advice for 2e rules stuff anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T12:49:00-07:00","id":456146,"title":"","content":"The athletics portion of defense is part of the issue. I understand it in some circumstances, though not others. The Brawling/Weaponry Dodge merits go a long way in helping it go down easier (or houseruling brawl for defense against brawl, weaponry for weaponry, athletics for thrown objects). It's weird that my procyclist character has more defense than my friend's boxer.<br /> <br /> I also don't like the dodge system, because as I understand it, dodging is usually just less effective than using your normal defense (if I'm wrong about that I'd love to better understand that system). That is perhaps the most counter intuitive aspect of the system for me.<br /> <br /> And then I just don't like how much it slows down battles. Battles are already long enough as is, increasing defense (about double for most of the character in our campaign) just doesn't seem necessary. This along with decreased dice pools due to automatic damage on weapons just doesn't seem like it'll lead to efficient play. <br /> <br /> And then in general, I just think fighting privileges the attacker over the defender. Almost universally, so it made sense before that it was easier to increase offense than defense. So I don't know. It just doesn't track for me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T13:56:35-07:00","id":456213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455271-converting-your-1e-game-to-2e?p=456146#post456146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The athletics portion of defense is part of the issue. I understand it in some circumstances, though not others. The Brawling/Weaponry Dodge merits go a long way in helping it go down easier (or houseruling brawl for defense against brawl, weaponry for weaponry, athletics for thrown objects). It's weird that my procyclist character has more defense than my friend's boxer.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty common complaint from what I've seen. It mostly comes from the abstraction of Skills. But your house rule there works pretty well, or you can just not add a Skill to Defense, since you also don't like the higher defenses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455271-converting-your-1e-game-to-2e?p=456146#post456146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also don't like the dodge system, because as I understand it, dodging is usually just less effective than using your normal defense (if I'm wrong about that I'd love to better understand that system). That is perhaps the most counter intuitive aspect of the system for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dodging took me a couple of reads to understand (&quot;wait, so you can either use Defense normally or roll double it as a dice pool? Wouldn't that leave you with lower Defense value on average?&quot;). It's important to remember though, defense only reduces your opponent's dice pool. Each success on your dodge roll cancels out one of your opponent's successes on their attack roll. So if your Defense isn't enough to reduce your opponent's dice pool below 3, they're still most likely to get one success, and then they're going do a bunch of damage from their weapon. But if you Dodge, you can keep them from doing any damage if you roll equal or more successes than your attacker. And even if you don't, you'll still at least reduce the damage somewhat, whereas static Defense is all-or-nothing. (This also conveniently addresses the &quot;no grazing blows&quot; problem.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455271-converting-your-1e-game-to-2e?p=456146#post456146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then I just don't like how much it slows down battles. Battles are already long enough as is, increasing defense (about double for most of the character in our campaign) just doesn't seem necessary. This along with decreased dice pools due to automatic damage on weapons just doesn't seem like it'll lead to efficient play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a matter of the new system requiring different combat tactics than the old system. You can't just roll dice until someone gets enough 8's 9's or 10's to fill up the other guy's health boxes any more. You have to use the environment to gain advantages, you have to focus your party's attacks on a single opponent to reduce their Defense, you have to spend Willpower to increase your attack dice pools, you have to apply Tilts, etc. This system can be just as efficient, but the players have to use different tactics than they may be used to, and the ST has to be willing to hand out situational bonuses and penalties. Of course, not everyone likes that style, so like I said earlier you could just leave out the +Athletics to Defense and combat will likely go much faster.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455271-converting-your-1e-game-to-2e?p=456146#post456146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then in general, I just think fighting privileges the attacker over the defender. Almost universally, so it made sense before that it was easier to increase offense than defense. So I don't know. It just doesn't track for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does. In the old system and in the new system, a fight between equally matched opponents always favors the attacker, although admittedly somewhat moreso in the old system. It seems like most of your issues revolve around Defense, so I would say just try without adding Athletics to Defense.<br /> <br /> Also, have you tried out the Down and Dirty Combat rules and/or the Beaten Down and Surrender rules? These help streamline combat tremendously when the combat is against unimportant mooks or when the goal is something other than carnage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-24-2015, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T14:09:47-07:00","id":456218,"title":"","content":"My game is fairly far along, I've run six stories each between 6 and 10 hours long with about that many left in the chronicle arch. I haven't converted over - still reading and creating my own sheets - but my plan is to go through the list of each stat from attributes to primal urge and convert every extra dot, merit, gift over to experience (2e experience). Then with the new sheet we'll create our characters as if new and my players can spend that experience to advance their characters. I won't however convert Renown to experience, I'll take each dot beyond the initial 3 and let them 'spend' their Renown differently so they can qualify for the Gifts they want. Within reason anyway, I'm not going to let the Blood Talon Rahu who's never been close to gaining Wisdom renown in game suddenly have 4 dots in it.<br /> <br /> I'll let them - within reason - go however they want to with their new experience, so long as they stick to the theme of their (old) characters. Hell even if they want to change Tribe because they don't like the idea of hunting people as Iron Masters, no problem. So long as they aren't suddenly RP'ing entirely different people.<br /> <br /> In regards to the whole 'never have grazing shots' argument.. the idea of a bullet wound that is just a deep scratch being a 'grazing shot' is a movie &amp; TV myth. The real power of a moderate-caliber bullet isn't so much the bullet itself, it's in the shockwave. In reality a 'grazing shot' is a serious flesh-wound. A real grazing shot is a bullet that missed but left a wound from the shockwave. If you want a more movie-style gun-play in your game there are certainly options available, house rules, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","user":"Xaielao","date":". 03-24-2015, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T14:27:21-07:00","id":456225,"title":"","content":"But then why change from the old system at all if I'm not adding athletics to defense? What aspect of the 2nd ed system are you advocating for? What change works better? Is it the damage that's been added to weapons? The initiative? Do either of those things change the system for the better?<br /> <br /> I literally love all aspects about 2nd edition but the combat changes, so I would really like to change my opinions on this. I'd rather just adopt the whole system, but it just doesn't work for me.<br /> <br /> Your points about the dodge do make sense, but I mean dodge sacrifices an attack action. That feels so much less effective and so rarely worth the choice and it makes choosing to defend such a risky move that rarely breaks you more than even. I don't know. The dodge is a real sticking point for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T14:55:01-07:00","id":456235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xaielao</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455271-converting-your-1e-game-to-2e?p=456218#post456218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My game is fairly far along, I've run six stories each between 6 and 10 hours long with about that many left in the chronicle arch. I haven't converted over - still reading and creating my own sheets - but my plan is to go through the list of each stat from attributes to primal urge and convert every extra dot, merit, gift over to experience (2e experience). Then with the new sheet we'll create our characters as if new and my players can spend that experience to advance their characters. I won't however convert Renown to experience, I'll take each dot beyond the initial 3 and let them 'spend' their Renown differently so they can qualify for the Gifts they want. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I like this idea but that requires a lot of work and I feel like my ST and I want to make things as painless as possible for some of our players who are newer to roleplaying games/less capable with the character sheet/experience aspect of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T15:53:33-07:00","id":456282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455271-converting-your-1e-game-to-2e?p=456225#post456225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then why change from the old system at all if I'm not adding athletics to defense? What aspect of the 2nd ed system are you advocating for? What change works better? Is it the damage that's been added to weapons? The initiative? Do either of those things change the system for the better?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a big fan of the damage from weapons and the damage reduction from armor, yeah. Along with Tilts, they improve combat a lot for me. I could take or leave Initiative modifiers and Athletics to Defense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455271-converting-your-1e-game-to-2e?p=456225#post456225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I literally love all aspects about 2nd edition but the combat changes, so I would really like to change my opinions on this. I'd rather just adopt the whole system, but it just doesn't work for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you tried it as written? It plays better than it reads, in my experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455271-converting-your-1e-game-to-2e?p=456225#post456225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your points about the dodge do make sense, but I mean dodge sacrifices an attack action. That feels so much less effective and so rarely worth the choice and it makes choosing to defend such a risky move that rarely breaks you more than even. I don't know. The dodge is a real sticking point for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>How often do you see players Dodge in the 1e combat system?<br /> <br /> Also, don't forget you don't dodge as your Instant action on your turn any more. You activate it Reflexively and lose your next action. So yes, it is situational, but you can hold off until the situation actually arises. If you get targeted by an attack that has 3 or more dice after your Defense, great! use your Dodge. If it gets all the way back around to your turn and you haven't been attacked, or your attackers only had small pools, great! Go ahead and attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T15:56:13-07:00","id":456284,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest trying the combat elements of the new system in play. I was very dubious about them back when they were first introduced in the GMC update, but I have been happily using them since - and they work extremely well for Werewolf in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T20:12:31-07:00","id":456517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455271-converting-your-1e-game-to-2e?p=456225#post456225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then why change from the old system at all if I'm not adding athletics to defense? What aspect of the 2nd ed system are you advocating for? What change works better? Is it the damage that's been added to weapons? The initiative? Do either of those things change the system for the better?<br /> <br /> I literally love all aspects about 2nd edition but the combat changes, so I would really like to change my opinions on this. I'd rather just adopt the whole system, but it just doesn't work for me.<br /> <br /> Your points about the dodge do make sense, but I mean dodge sacrifices an attack action. That feels so much less effective and so rarely worth the choice and it makes choosing to defend such a risky move that rarely breaks you more than even. I don't know. The dodge is a real sticking point for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from the obvious changes with weapon damage, initiative modifiers and that they always deal lethal? I'd say one of the best improvements would be how the fighting style merits were changed to mesh with these new rules. Defensive styles that if you reduce your attacker's successes to 0 while dodging makes you redirect the attack to a nearby opponent (unarmed defense) is a lot better than it was. Also, with higher defense comes higher dodge DP. I've made quite a few characters who reached 14 dices on dodge rolls. <br /> <br /> Some maneuvers also inflict an automatic Tilt. Instead of dodging, you use Strength + Brawl and should you score more successes than your attacker, you do your extra successes as damage and inflict an automatic Arm Wrack (drop item held and suffer off hand penalties on most rools) or Leg Wrack (Half speed &amp; -2 penalty on physical rools in regards to movement).<br /> <br /> In short, I find making defensive PC who know how to fight to be much more useful than in the 1E system. (Plus, I recently played a type of peaceful monk that always preaches peace and diplomacy but would love to humiliate street punks who tried to gang up on him)<br /> <br /> As for high defense players being a problem, I like to use my &quot;sand in the eyes&quot; tactic. Blinded Tilt on both eyes for number of turn equal to successes on a Dexterity + Athletics roll and... POOF! No more Defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4990-de_k47","name":"De_K47","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4990_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T05:30:04-07:00","id":456757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455271-converting-your-1e-game-to-2e?p=456284#post456284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd suggest trying the combat elements of the new system in play. I was very dubious about them back when they were first introduced in the GMC update, but I have been happily using them since - and they work extremely well for Werewolf in particular.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Concur this, SOOO MUCH - Conditions and Tilts need to get used to, but adds intense and clear picture of fight. Higher Defence from Athletics mean that non-combat oriented characters still can survive the fight - my <b>Mage</b> players do not invest in Weaponry or Firearms that are illogical for them, but Athletics higher in battle scared librarian is much more plausible. And going with 0 Attack Dicepools means that players try to inflict the Tilts, and those add drama and nice description to the fights.<br /> <br /> Yes, new system is a little bit more complicated - but it's even more evocative and fun in play. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-25-2015, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T14:07:27-07:00","id":457275,"title":"","content":"If you're in a game that will have an ending and people will make new characters for the next story, just finish out with the rules you have. If it's long-term, or &quot;persistent world&quot; setting, or something where people keep their characters across multiple stories, then you have a couple options. The easiest is, if there's a break between stories, use that time to rewrite the characters. If there's no break, you'll have to create one or specify a conversion time where characters are re-written into the new system.<br /> <br /> As far as conversion: Take existing characters, calculate their spent experience point cost total, take total and divide by 5, then remake characters from the ground up with the new rules and the converted Experiences. My game already did this once for the GMC/VTR2 conversion, and now we're going to have to do a similar &quot;template shift&quot; for WTF2 (as in, the WTF characters already converted to GMC, we just have to re-convert gifts, rites, and wolf-blooded).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}